.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH byssus 8  "byssus 0.1.0" "Byssus Manual"
.SH NAME
byssus \- Byssus command\-line tool: inspect, validate and reconcile mounts
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbyssus\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-level\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Byssus command\-line tool: inspect, validate and reconcile mounts.
.PP
status, dry\-run and check never mount anything; run as root with daemon.user configured, they look as that user, as the daemon would. reconcile performs one reconciliation pass and needs CAP_SYS_ADMIN.
.PP
See also byssusd(8), and REFERENCE.md and OPERATIONS.md in /usr/share/doc/byssus.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Main configuration file [default: /etc/byssus/byssus.toml]
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Drop\-in configuration directory [default: /etc/byssus/conf.d]
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR
Log level for diagnostics on stderr: error, warn, info, debug, trace
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
byssus\-status(8)
Show every desired or recorded member and its mount state
.TP
byssus\-dry\-run(8)
Validate configuration, kernel, permissions and propagation, and show what a reconcile would do, without mounting anything
.TP
byssus\-reconcile(8)
Perform one reconciliation pass and exit. Requires CAP_SYS_ADMIN and refuses to run while byssusd holds the state lock
.TP
byssus\-check(8)
Check whether the configuration would be accepted by a reload, optionally with drop\-in fragments added, replaced or removed, without installing anything or signaling the daemon
.TP
byssus\-version(8)
Print the version
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
